{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore carries a tight ISO fit tolerance of 0.018 mm, but the drawing does not account for the added thickness of the I.Z.B.P. plating; after plating the hole will be undersize and the mating shaft may not assemble. The designer should either reduce the pre-plate hole size to leave room for the coating or add a note specifying reaming/machining after plating."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Reduce the nominal/tolerance of D12 before plating to allow for the I.Z.B.P. thickness, or add a note requiring the hole to be finished to size after plating."}]}
